    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0418" n="1096" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1096"/>

                <head>Mr. Pruyn to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 27.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Yedo</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-05-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 12, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> England and France have offered to assist
                    the Tycoon against the hostile daimios. The offer will probably be declined.
                    Then coercive measures will follow. The United States steamer Wyoming is at
                    Kanagawa.</p>
                <p>I have honor to be, sir, your most obedient, humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident, &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p>The above is a copy of the despatch sent to the collector at San Francisco,
                        to be sent by telegraph to Washington.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
